# Screen structure & responsive layout

When creating or updating screens under `src/screens/`, follow this structure and responsive approach.

## Folder layout

```
src/screens/FeatureScreen/
  FeatureScreen.tsx          # screen shell, navigation, selectors, composition
  styles.ts                  # screen-level styles only
  data.ts                    # pure helpers, filters, builders (no JSX)
  hooks/                     # feature hooks (optional)
  useFeatureLayout.ts        # optional; prefer shared hook below
  components/
    index.ts                 # public exports
    SomeCard.tsx
    SomeCard.styles.ts
    SomeCard.data.ts         # heavy pure logic for that component (optional)
```

- Keep `*Screen.tsx` thin: wire state, pass props, compose components.
- Colocate styles as `ComponentName.styles.ts`.
- Put pure logic in `data.ts` / `*.data.ts` — no React, no styles.
- Export public pieces from `components/index.ts`.

## Responsive layout (phone / tablet / Mac)

Use `useResponsiveLayout` from `src/hooks/useResponsiveLayout.ts`:

- `compact` — phone; horizontal scroll for dense tables/stat strips is OK
- `tablet` / `desktop` — stretch columns, wrap filters, 2-column card grids, larger padding
- Apply `contentPadding` + `contentMaxWidth` on the screen `ScrollView` `contentContainerStyle`
- Center content with `alignSelf: 'center'` + `width: '100%'` when `contentMaxWidth` is set

## Tables & heatmaps

- Measure available width (`onLayout` or `viewportWidth`)
- If `available >= minWidth` → flex columns fill width (no horizontal scroll)
- Else → fixed min widths + horizontal `ScrollView`
- Do not hardcode phone-only fixed layouts for tablet/Mac

## Do / Don't

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — giant screen file with inline StyleSheet + fixed table widths only
// ❌ BAD — duplicate breakpoint logic per screen

// ✅ GOOD — Screen composes cards; cards own styles; data.ts owns builders
// ✅ GOOD — shared useResponsiveLayout; tables stretch when wide
```
